  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<div>The proposed development, by reason of its design, bulk, mass, scale and siting, would appear incongruous and out of keeping with the prevailing character of the host dwelling and semi-detached pair and the distinctiveness and historic character of the Becontree Estate. The proposal would result in a detrimental loss of symmetry of the existing pair of dwellings. The proposal would result in the loss of the open aspect to the corner plot which would have a significantly harmful impact on the character and appearance of the area,&nbsp;therefore causing detrimental harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character:</div><div><br></div><div><ul><li style=\"\">National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024) </li><li style=\"\">Policies&nbsp;D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) </li><li style=\"\">The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) </li><li style=\"\">Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)</li></ul></div>"
  ],
